<i>A clean kill. No mistakes.</i>

40:51.798 --> 40:57.128
<i>Now, I have another deal,
a side part, for you.</i>

40:57.136 --> 40:59.136
<i>Okay, go on.</i>

40:59.138 --> 41:01.138
<i>When you've
executed the contract,</i>

41:01.140 --> 41:05.640
<i>I want you
to kill your partner.</i>

41:05.644 --> 41:07.044
Why?

41:07.046 --> 41:08.576
<i>I don't like crowds.</i>

41:08.582 --> 41:12.652
<i>And I like loyalty I can buy.</i>

41:12.651 --> 41:16.021
<i>Double the original offer,
in cash.</i>

41:18.925 --> 41:22.025
What you want,
his head on a silver platter?

41:22.028 --> 41:25.998
<i>His ID papers and
trigger finger will suffice.</i>

41:25.999 --> 41:29.799
<i>I'm offering you double
the money and a one way split.</i>

41:29.803 --> 41:34.043
<i>I believe I can trust
your mercenary greed.</i>

41:34.039 --> 41:36.939
<i>Now, do we have a deal?</i>

41:38.845 --> 41:40.205
Yeah.

41:40.213 --> 41:41.913
Consider it done.

41:41.914 --> 41:44.024
<i>Good.</i>

41:48.722 --> 41:50.792
Where'd you get ahold
of that there thing?

41:50.789 --> 41:53.089
Where the fuck
did you get that?

41:53.093 --> 41:55.093
Stop it, Alfred.
He's just the messenger.

41:55.095 --> 41:57.685
Who is about to get very shot
on the count of three.

41:57.696 --> 41:59.996
One, two...

41:59.999 --> 42:02.929
Locker!
Locker in the terminal!

42:02.935 --> 42:05.035
Black briefcase.

42:05.037 --> 42:06.097
Note inside.

42:06.106 --> 42:08.066
A man...
A man paid me.

42:08.073 --> 42:10.913
An envelope with money.

42:10.910 --> 42:12.180
Please don't kill me!

42:12.178 --> 42:14.008
Three.

42:17.182 --> 42:19.752
Now fuck off.

42:19.752 --> 42:21.222
Go on.

42:25.691 --> 42:27.191
Fuck!

42:29.896 --> 42:33.696
Fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck!

42:33.700 --> 42:35.700
Fucker!

42:38.238 --> 42:40.168
Feel better?

42:42.876 --> 42:45.836
It's all bullshit, isn't it?

42:45.845 --> 42:48.375
No job, no hit.

42:48.381 --> 42:50.251
Oh, no, handsome.

42:52.285 --> 42:55.385
There most definitely was a hit.

42:57.856 --> 42:59.016
Me?

42:59.024 --> 43:00.794
Not anymore.

43:00.794 --> 43:03.134
We can find a new target.

43:04.897 --> 43:06.297
We?

43:06.298 --> 43:09.198
Now tell me something,
sugarplum.

43:09.202 --> 43:12.842
Why should I trust you, eh?

43:12.839 --> 43:16.209
Aren't you part of
this whole conspiracy?

43:16.209 --> 43:18.879
I told you.

43:19.946 --> 43:22.276
I like you.

43:22.281 --> 43:25.151
I need someone
to butter my buns for.

43:32.425 --> 43:35.825
Well, I suppose I do need
a new partner now, don't I?

43:35.828 --> 43:40.458
My old one seems to have
become rather untrustworthy.

43:40.466 --> 43:42.426
But I will warn you, Alfred.

43:42.435 --> 43:45.865
I'll need a firm hand and a
regular lash of the tongue.

43:45.872 --> 43:49.272
I can't wait
to have you under me.

43:49.274 --> 43:51.014
Good.

43:51.010 --> 43:54.080
Let's have a cup of tea
and plot our bloody revenge.

43:54.080 --> 43:58.480
You tidy that up.
I'll put the kettle on...

43:58.484 --> 43:59.924
partner.

44:10.196 --> 44:13.896
The way I see it,
you've got two options.

44:13.899 --> 44:14.929
Go on.

44:14.934 --> 44:16.834
Option A: suicide.

44:16.836 --> 44:18.496
I see. And B?

44:18.504 --> 44:21.044
Well, you've got to hear
the case for Option A first.

44:21.039 --> 44:23.209
- I do?
- You do.

44:23.209 --> 44:24.479
I'm all ears.

44:24.477 --> 44:26.307
- You're dying.
- Apparently.

44:26.312 --> 44:28.912
- You're not happy about it.
- Not really.

44:28.914 --> 44:30.414
You're miserable, touchy.

44:30.415 --> 44:32.775
Quite frankly,
not great company.

44:32.785 --> 44:34.045
Oh, thank you.

44:34.053 --> 44:35.553
Want my advice?

44:35.555 --> 44:36.885
No.

44:38.857 --> 44:40.557
Just end it.

44:40.560 --> 44:43.360
Have you ever considered
counseling?

44:43.363 --> 44:45.063
Every minute of every day,

44:45.064 --> 44:46.834
you're bombarded with
a series of hazardous

44:46.832 --> 44:49.572
and potentially life-ending
situations to choose from.

44:49.568 --> 44:51.568
Jump in front of a bus.

44:51.571 --> 44:53.141
Have a bath with your toaster.

44:53.138 --> 44:54.498
Fall on your butter knife.

44:54.506 --> 44:56.506
Tall buildings,
rivers, bridges, trains.

44:56.508 --> 44:58.138
There are more ways
to end your life

44:58.144 --> 45:00.414
than there are ways to live it.

45:00.412 --> 45:02.412
All this pissing around
in train stations

45:02.414 --> 45:04.054
in the middle of the night
would be over.

45:04.050 --> 45:07.480
End this nothing,
and all it takes is some balls.

45:07.486 --> 45:10.186
And my immortal soul?

45:10.189 --> 45:11.919
Overrated.

45:11.925 --> 45:14.455
Overrated?

45:14.459 --> 45:19.799
Have you done something to put
your immortal soul in jeopardy?

45:24.604 --> 45:28.944
Well, there you go then.
Nothing to worry about.

45:28.941 --> 45:30.171
Are you Catholic?

45:30.176 --> 45:31.376
Yeah.

45:33.580 --> 45:35.410
Religious?

45:37.584 --> 45:40.984
Oh, fuck me.
Oh, sorry. Um...

45:40.986 --> 45:43.486
Forgive me, Father,
for I have sinned.

45:43.488 --> 45:45.918
To be honest, I can't recall
the last time I took confession.

45:45.925 --> 45:49.925
I think it's more than 10,
but less than 20.

45:49.928 --> 45:51.188
Days?

45:51.196 --> 45:55.266
Months?
Not years, surely.

45:55.267 --> 45:56.997
Don't get pissed off at me
for telling you the truth.

45:57.002 --> 45:58.972
That's just mean.

45:58.972 --> 46:01.102
If I'd known you were like this,
I would've just said three days

46:01.106 --> 46:03.436
and taken my chances
with the Almighty.

46:03.443 --> 46:05.283
Sorry.

46:06.613 --> 46:09.083
That was uncalled for.
I apologize.

46:11.251 --> 46:13.481
Are you still there?

46:15.120 --> 46:17.960
I know you're there.
I can smell sherry.

46:19.158 --> 46:20.558
Define religious.

46:20.560 --> 46:22.000
Lolly?

46:23.562 --> 46:26.462
I'll take that
as a big fat no.

46:26.466 --> 46:28.926
Maybe it's divine retribution.

46:28.935 --> 46:31.595
Oh, yeah, that sounds tasty.

46:31.604 --> 46:34.604
You know,
my sins revisiting me

46:34.606 --> 46:37.376
and my past
coming back to haunt me...

46:37.377 --> 46:40.977
I'm all ears, William.

46:40.979 --> 46:43.049
Let me hear your confession.

46:51.457 --> 46:53.987
Repent and thou shalt be saved!

46:55.528 --> 46:57.188
That's not even from the Bible.

46:57.196 --> 46:59.056
Okay, that is the graffiti

46:59.064 --> 47:01.934
that's written on the bus stop
opposite the terminal.

47:01.935 --> 47:03.495
That's disappointing.

47:03.502 --> 47:06.002
That's pretty much my entire
knowledge of scripture.

47:06.004 --> 47:08.044
Try this one:
Repent, turn back,

47:08.040 --> 47:10.370
and thy sins
will be blotted out.

47:10.376 --> 47:12.206
Not really as catchy, is it?

47:14.046 --> 47:15.676
How's my case
for suicide progressing?

47:15.682 --> 47:17.212
Am I quaking your foundations?

47:17.216 --> 47:19.116
You're giving me a headache.

47:19.118 --> 47:21.118
Oh, how's this for a headache?

47:21.120 --> 47:23.690
Take a pencil,
jam into tabletop,

47:23.689 --> 47:27.019
slam head down onto pencil,
dead in five seconds.

47:27.026 --> 47:28.726
- That's foul.
- Isn't it?

47:28.727 --> 47:30.257
And every time
I suggest this to someone,

47:30.263 --> 47:31.733
they think it goes
up your nose.

47:31.731 --> 47:33.501
You've suggested this
more than once?

47:33.499 --> 47:35.499
It can't go up your nose.
That's impossible.

47:35.501 --> 47:37.471
Think about
the trajectory involved.

47:37.470 --> 47:39.100
It would go in your eyeball,
right?

47:39.104 --> 47:40.744
Through the socket,
into your brain.

47:40.740 --> 47:44.440
I... Well, it depends on the
angle of the head, I suppose.

47:44.443 --> 47:46.143
Let's test the theory.

47:46.144 --> 47:49.014
It's not very sharp, is it?

47:49.015 --> 47:50.115
Use your fancy pen then.

47:52.452 --> 47:53.522
It's heavier.

47:53.519 --> 47:56.419
Nib's sharper than yours.

47:56.421 --> 47:59.461
Probably get it further into
the table, better purchase.

48:01.127 --> 48:03.187
It would feel more proper,
wouldn't it?

48:03.196 --> 48:04.556
More ceremonial.

48:04.564 --> 48:08.064
A pen does have more purpose
than a pencil.

48:08.066 --> 48:09.226
More stature.

48:09.234 --> 48:10.704
Definitely a better choice.

48:10.702 --> 48:13.672
Definitely,
and how resonantly poetic.

48:13.673 --> 48:17.043
The English professor found
impaled on his own fountain pen.

48:17.042 --> 48:18.042
It's epic.

48:18.044 --> 48:19.084
It's inspired.

48:19.077 --> 48:20.407
We've cracked it!

48:20.412 --> 48:24.082
Time, place, method,
it's all there.

48:24.082 --> 48:26.082
Don't you think
it'd be a bit painful?

48:26.084 --> 48:27.584
You're missing the point.

48:27.586 --> 48:29.046
Hmm?

48:29.055 --> 48:30.615
Get it?

48:30.622 --> 48:32.792
- Brilliant.
- God, you're not very keen.

48:32.792 --> 48:34.522
Do you want to
kill yourself or not?

48:34.526 --> 48:35.726
I'm not so sure now.

48:35.727 --> 48:37.657
Oh, pathetic.

48:37.662 --> 48:39.662
Can I have that pen then?
I never had one like that.

48:39.664 --> 48:41.234
- No.
- Why?

48:41.234 --> 48:43.574
Because it's mine.

48:43.568 --> 48:45.198
Thought you were
about to top yourself?

48:45.203 --> 48:46.743
What do you need a pen for?

48:46.738 --> 48:48.708
Come on, please. It'll be
like you left it for me.

48:48.707 --> 48:50.537
- Bequeathed it, not left.
- Oh, my God.

48:50.542 --> 48:52.312
Shut up!
I'm taking the pen.

48:52.310 --> 48:54.280
You've got no use for it,
and I want it.

48:54.280 --> 48:56.450
Here, you can have my pencil
to make up for your loss, okay?

48:56.448 --> 48:58.548
Done, swapped, over.

49:20.106 --> 49:22.706
<i>How long have
we been stuck in here?</i>

49:24.843 --> 49:29.153
<i>12 days, 13 hours,
and 27 minutes. Why?</i>

49:29.147 --> 49:30.707
<i>Just wondering.</i>

49:30.716 --> 49:32.376
<i>You missing
your bottle blonde?</i>

49:32.385 --> 49:34.845
Geez, you're like
a hormonal teenager.

49:34.854 --> 49:37.654
She's gonna be the death of you,
that fucking girl.

49:37.656 --> 49:39.816
- Cards.
- Yeah?

49:39.825 --> 49:42.485
- Great. Hold 'em.
- Three-card brag.

49:42.495 --> 49:44.355
Fuck off.
That's a pouf's game.

49:44.363 --> 49:46.163
Fine. Hold 'em it is.

49:46.164 --> 49:47.874
Fair enough. Let's go!

49:47.867 --> 49:49.467
That's more like it.

49:49.468 --> 49:51.098
Oh, give 'em here.

49:51.104 --> 49:52.374
You're gonna fucking
hurt yourself. Come on.

49:52.370 --> 49:53.810
Just give 'em to me.

49:55.774 --> 49:57.274
For fuck's sake, Alf.

49:57.276 --> 49:59.746
There's fucking
barely half a deck.

50:03.515 --> 50:05.315
We could always play snap.

50:05.318 --> 50:07.618
I'll snap your fucking neck
in a minute!

50:09.856 --> 50:12.686
How do you play solitaire?

50:12.691 --> 50:16.561
Quietly, on your own,
in the other fucking room.

50:16.562 --> 50:19.162
- You really are becoming a...
- Yeah, a fucking liability.

50:19.164 --> 50:21.074
I know. Hear it all the time.

50:26.772 --> 50:29.542
Boss, look at this.

50:29.542 --> 50:30.842
What is it?

50:30.843 --> 50:32.613
Something for me
to beat you to death with?

50:32.611 --> 50:33.681
No.

50:35.680 --> 50:39.250
"The time has come,
the walrus said,

50:39.252 --> 50:40.852
to talk of many things.

50:40.852 --> 50:45.622
<i>Of shoes
and ships and sealing wax,</i>

50:45.624 --> 50:47.664
of cabbages and kings."

50:47.660 --> 50:52.170
"And why the sea is boiling hot
and whether pigs have wings."

50:53.499 --> 50:54.829
I don't get it.

50:54.834 --> 50:57.174
It's gibberish.

50:57.169 --> 50:59.469
It's all like this,
the whole bloody book.

50:59.472 --> 51:01.342
It's just fucking drivel.

51:01.339 --> 51:04.379
Well, I'm sure Lewis Carroll
will be suitably apologetic

51:04.377 --> 51:07.537
when he finds out
how upset you are.

51:07.546 --> 51:09.646
Why don't you fuck off
into the other room

51:09.649 --> 51:11.819
and leave me alone, eh?

51:31.336 --> 51:33.366
Want a drink?

51:33.372 --> 51:35.272
A proper drink, I mean.

51:35.274 --> 51:37.144
Oh, no doubt.

51:40.946 --> 51:43.706
Bill, it's time
we explore Option B.

51:43.716 --> 51:44.976
Oh, goody, there's more.

51:44.984 --> 51:46.254
There is.

51:46.252 --> 51:49.722
Option B: assisted suicide.

51:50.957 --> 51:53.417
I believe they call that
"euthanasia."

51:53.426 --> 51:54.756
Eutha-what?

51:54.760 --> 51:57.600
It was very popular at one time
with the Swiss.

51:57.597 --> 51:58.627
What's a Swiss?

52:00.499 --> 52:01.999
Doesn't matter.

52:02.001 --> 52:03.771
All I'm saying is,

52:03.769 --> 52:06.239
if you haven't got the peanuts
to do it yourself,

52:06.238 --> 52:08.238
just get someone
to do it for you.

52:08.240 --> 52:10.310
Are you saying I take
a contract out on myself?

52:10.309 --> 52:12.009
Exactly.

52:12.010 --> 52:14.440
Do they have an assassins
section in the classifieds?

52:14.446 --> 52:16.676
"Wanted: tall, dark,
anonymous stranger.

52:16.682 --> 52:18.252
Must have own rifle."

52:18.251 --> 52:19.651
My new boyfriend's
a contract killer.

52:23.256 --> 52:24.956
And, talk about
getting lucky,

52:24.957 --> 52:26.357
he's getting off
a job today.

52:26.359 --> 52:27.919
Serendipity, indeed.

52:27.926 --> 52:29.856
We could give him
a brief, you know,

52:29.861 --> 52:31.961
suggest a few ways
you wouldn't mind being killed,

52:31.964 --> 52:34.374
let him pick the best one.

52:34.367 --> 52:36.267
Try this on for size.

52:36.269 --> 52:39.299
You're just going about your
daily business, then one day,

52:39.305 --> 52:41.465
you're on your way home from
a long day in the classroom...

52:42.607 --> 52:44.737
Shot in the head.

52:44.743 --> 52:46.713
Last thing
you would've expected.

52:46.711 --> 52:49.481
I think it's safe to say
if I'd paid somebody to kill me,

52:49.481 --> 52:52.621
I'd be expecting to be killed
most of the time.

52:52.618 --> 52:55.548
You just have to, you know,
try not to think about it.

52:55.553 --> 52:57.853
- Oh, okay, I'll do that then.
- Right.

52:57.856 --> 52:59.686
Can we bank long distance
head shots then?

52:59.691 --> 53:01.831
Quick, anonymous, painless.

53:01.827 --> 53:03.427
- Sounds like a keeper.
- Great.

53:03.428 --> 53:04.898
Let's brainstorm
a few more ways to die.

53:04.897 --> 53:05.867
Let's!

53:09.669 --> 53:11.769
- Stabbing?
- No, I don't like knives.

53:11.771 --> 53:14.041
It sounds very,
sort of messy and painful.

53:14.039 --> 53:16.439
That's the sort of thing
he's gonna need to know.

53:16.441 --> 53:18.641
- Who?
- Our possibly fictitious,

53:18.644 --> 53:19.914
but possibly real hit man,

53:19.912 --> 53:20.982
who happens to be
my new boyfriend.

53:20.979 --> 53:22.579
Oh, okay.

53:22.580 --> 53:25.950
Ooh, what about a hit and run?

53:30.656 --> 53:33.586
Oh, now, I have a problem
with that.

53:33.591 --> 53:35.691
- Go on.
- What if I just get mangled?

53:35.694 --> 53:38.864
He'd have to reverse
back over me.

53:38.863 --> 53:41.103
That's just horrifying.

53:41.100 --> 53:42.930
Hmm.

53:42.935 --> 53:45.335
- Pushing?
- I don't follow.

53:45.338 --> 53:47.338
Off a tall building,
for the sake of argument,

53:47.339 --> 53:49.409
or in front of a train.

53:49.408 --> 53:53.638
I must say I have explored
the idea of trains somewhat.

53:53.646 --> 53:55.776
Hey!

53:58.050 --> 54:00.080
Short, sticky, and sweet.
Before you know it,

54:00.086 --> 54:02.346
you're strawberry jam
and dental fillings.

54:02.354 --> 54:03.924
You really can
paint a picture, Annie.

54:03.923 --> 54:05.823
Only downside's the whole
closed casket thing.

54:05.825 --> 54:08.755
Granted, but I am starting
to like the idea of falling.

54:08.760 --> 54:10.890
It sounds almost accidental.

54:10.896 --> 54:12.756
Can we bank it, pushing?

54:12.765 --> 54:14.425
Yeah, let's have it.

54:14.432 --> 54:16.072
To imminent death.

54:16.068 --> 54:17.668
To the 404.

54:31.484 --> 54:32.494
What's up?

54:33.919 --> 54:35.119
What?

54:35.120 --> 54:37.850
Is there anything
you want to say?

54:37.856 --> 54:39.326
No.

54:48.401 --> 54:49.871
I'm seriously fucking bored.

54:49.868 --> 54:51.538
You want to play a game?

54:51.537 --> 54:53.567
Do I look like I play
Snakes and Ladders to you?

54:53.571 --> 54:55.681
Well, you did do that jigsaw.

54:58.510 --> 54:59.710
I fucking hate puzzles.

54:59.711 --> 55:01.551
You did do that crossword book.

55:03.182 --> 55:05.082
- You trying to be funny?
- What about chess?

55:07.952 --> 55:10.652
- Are you trying to be funny?
- No, Boss.

55:10.656 --> 55:13.656
So I don't have to come over and
teach you some fucking manners.

55:13.658 --> 55:15.158
- No, Boss.
- Because if I do

55:15.160 --> 55:18.730
you're gonna fucking regret it,
you understand me?

55:18.731 --> 55:20.501
Yes, Boss.

55:26.604 --> 55:27.544
Good.

55:31.577 --> 55:34.137
Don't fancy Monopoly then?

55:34.146 --> 55:36.646
God, keep it up.

55:36.649 --> 55:39.679
I'm going to put you six feet
under the fucking ground, mate.

55:39.685 --> 55:42.115
Are you?

55:43.955 --> 55:46.155
You know, I don't know
why I bother on you.

55:46.158 --> 55:48.458
I should just shoot you
in the face,

55:48.461 --> 55:49.861
get myself another apprentice.

55:49.861 --> 55:51.931
I thought I was
a junior partner.

55:51.930 --> 55:55.800
Oh, that's just the flash way
of saying "apprentice."

55:55.801 --> 55:57.031
I'm a valuable asset.

55:57.035 --> 55:59.895
You're a fucking liability.

55:59.905 --> 56:02.535
I already told you what I do
with fucking liabilities.

56:02.540 --> 56:05.110
If it wasn't for me,
who'd make the tea,

56:05.109 --> 56:07.679
collect the cash,
sort the jobs?

56:07.680 --> 56:10.720
You know, do the fucking work!

56:13.752 --> 56:16.462
Good lad.
Now you're getting it.

56:38.843 --> 56:41.113
Oh, cracking.

56:41.113 --> 56:43.253
Pathetic fallacy.

56:43.249 --> 56:45.249
Whinging librarian.

56:45.251 --> 56:47.151
Excuse me?

56:47.151 --> 56:50.151
No, that's what that's called,
when emotional turmoil

56:50.155 --> 56:52.715
is reflected
in tangible surroundings.

56:52.725 --> 56:56.685
Like two lovers go their
separate ways in a rainstorm,

56:56.694 --> 56:59.964
or lightning strikes
as the murderer's revealed.

56:59.964 --> 57:01.564
It adds gravitas.

57:01.566 --> 57:03.166
It would hardly be
as nerve-wracking

57:03.167 --> 57:04.997
if the serial killer
stabbed his victim to death

57:05.004 --> 57:06.574
in a sunny park, would it?

57:06.571 --> 57:10.711
Much better in a dark alley
in a mist.

57:10.709 --> 57:14.309
My God, you are wasted
as a teacher.

57:14.312 --> 57:17.082
You should be published.

57:17.082 --> 57:18.752
You should be preaching.

57:18.751 --> 57:21.181
You should be inciting
bloody revolution.

57:21.185 --> 57:23.845
And yet here I am,
a lamenting English teacher

57:23.856 --> 57:26.016
coughing his spleen
out through his nose,

57:26.024 --> 57:29.264
wishing the earth
would swallow him whole.

57:36.135 --> 57:37.535
Come with me.

57:39.972 --> 57:41.112
Really?

57:42.207 --> 57:43.237
Bill!

57:47.046 --> 57:48.516
Oh!

57:56.287 --> 57:58.087
Where are we going?

57:58.089 --> 58:02.629
To explore gravitas
and pathetic fallacy.

58:02.627 --> 58:04.057
Chop, chop!

58:10.903 --> 58:12.943
Well, this seems
like a great idea.

58:12.937 --> 58:16.367
Come on, Bill.
Where's your sense of adventure?

58:16.374 --> 58:19.714
Warm and dry
and congealing with my coffee.

58:39.330 --> 58:41.370
What the hell is that?

58:41.367 --> 58:43.097
It's an old ventilation shaft

58:43.102 --> 58:45.302
from when the city actually
used to work properly.

58:45.303 --> 58:47.073
It's condemned now.

58:47.071 --> 58:49.871
Just a hole
dropping into nowhere.

58:49.874 --> 58:53.914
Down and down and down.

58:53.912 --> 58:56.982
Well, that's just about the most
terrifying thing I've ever seen.

58:56.981 --> 58:58.711
You come here often, do you?

58:58.716 --> 59:01.146
Oh, yes, I love it here.

59:01.153 --> 59:03.753
- Here, come stand on the edge.
- No, I...

59:03.756 --> 59:05.686
Close your eyes.

59:06.925 --> 59:09.155
Feels amazing.

59:10.729 --> 59:13.659
Annie, come on back.

59:13.665 --> 59:14.795
Oh, my God!

59:20.339 --> 59:21.439
Well?

59:21.439 --> 59:23.169
Well, what?

59:23.175 --> 59:25.165
You said you wanted the earth
to swallow you whole

59:25.176 --> 59:26.876
not five minutes ago.

59:26.879 --> 59:28.279
There you go.

59:28.280 --> 59:29.980
You're welcome.

59:31.249 --> 59:32.819
You want me to jump in there?

59:32.818 --> 59:34.318
Pathetic fallacy.

59:34.318 --> 59:36.818
- No, it's not.
- Yes, it is.

59:36.821 --> 59:39.761
Emotional turmoil reflected
in tangible surroundings.

59:39.758 --> 59:41.458
I'm in a deep, dark hole.

59:41.459 --> 59:43.789
It's perfect.

59:43.796 --> 59:45.256
Let's test your gravitas.

59:45.263 --> 59:48.033
- Or gravity, more like.
- Exactly!

59:48.033 --> 59:50.403
Look, I'm not gonna throw
myself into a yawning chasm

59:50.401 --> 59:52.271
just because it fits neatly
into a metaphor!

59:52.271 --> 59:55.001
Why not?
Quick, clean, painless.

59:55.006 --> 59:56.836
Poetically resonant.

59:56.841 --> 59:59.711
You are insane, certifiably.

59:59.711 --> 1:00:01.111
Unquestionably.
You get close to the edge,

1:00:01.113 --> 1:00:02.253
and then I can push you...

1:00:02.247 --> 1:00:04.777
Time out! Time out, okay?

1:00:04.783 --> 1:00:06.723
Okay, fine, fine.

1:00:10.122 --> 1:00:12.392
What the fuck was that?

1:00:12.390 --> 1:00:14.060
Are you out of
your fucking mind?

1:00:14.059 --> 1:00:16.129
What is the worst that
could've happened, Bill?

1:00:16.127 --> 1:00:18.827
You'd be dead.
It would all be over.

1:00:18.830 --> 1:00:20.900
No more pain,
no more suffering.

1:00:20.899 --> 1:00:22.899
No more waiting for a train
that isn't coming.

1:00:22.901 --> 1:00:25.301
What if I had just let you fall?

1:00:25.303 --> 1:00:27.143
None of this would be happening.

1:00:27.138 --> 1:00:30.038
This conversation,
your smoldering anger,

1:00:30.042 --> 1:00:32.242
your eloquent
bloody resentment.

1:00:32.243 --> 1:00:33.843
Nothing.

1:00:33.845 --> 1:00:36.405
Not like that.
I do not want to go like that.

1:00:36.414 --> 1:00:38.214
Like what, Bill?

1:00:38.216 --> 1:00:41.916
Trains, cars, gunshots,
it's all the same end product.

1:00:44.923 --> 1:00:48.393
I think the question
really is,

1:00:48.392 --> 1:00:52.292
do you want to go at all?

1:00:52.296 --> 1:00:56.366
Standing on the edge really
makes you think, doesn't it?

1:00:56.368 --> 1:00:58.028
I'll shoot you in the face.

1:00:58.035 --> 1:01:01.035
I wish you bloody would,
but you won't.

1:01:01.039 --> 1:01:05.079
Stop thinking, Bill.

1:01:05.077 --> 1:01:08.007
Stop reasoning.

1:01:08.013 --> 1:01:10.453
Just close your eyes.

1:01:10.448 --> 1:01:14.948
Take a last breath
and just walk.

1:01:18.856 --> 1:01:20.856
Clock's ticking.

1:01:20.859 --> 1:01:22.419
It's quiet out there.

1:01:22.426 --> 1:01:25.296
It's like
a fucking apocalypse.

1:01:35.039 --> 1:01:36.509
Just one round.

1:01:36.508 --> 1:01:37.838
What?

1:01:37.843 --> 1:01:39.883
I said there's no one around.

1:01:39.877 --> 1:01:41.477
Yeah, it's dead.

1:01:43.314 --> 1:01:46.054
Like a corpse.

1:01:53.258 --> 1:01:54.488
Was that loaded?

1:01:56.127 --> 1:01:57.587
Yeah.

1:01:57.595 --> 1:01:59.195
You're dead.

1:02:04.269 --> 1:02:06.069
Milk, two sugars.

1:02:07.138 --> 1:02:09.178
What are you waiting for?

1:02:26.457 --> 1:02:27.887
That's it.

1:02:38.336 --> 1:02:40.336
No. No, I can't.

1:02:42.406 --> 1:02:44.836
How disappointing.

1:02:47.578 --> 1:02:49.148
Disappointing?

1:02:51.515 --> 1:02:54.075
Disappointing?

1:02:54.086 --> 1:02:56.886
This is all a fucking game
to you, isn't it?

1:02:58.890 --> 1:03:01.490
Get this through
your little skull, okay?

1:03:01.493 --> 1:03:03.033
I am dying.

1:03:03.028 --> 1:03:05.398
I am...
I am going to die!

1:03:05.397 --> 1:03:07.927
To me, all this is real!

1:03:07.932 --> 1:03:11.232
The fucking hole
in the ground is real!

1:03:11.236 --> 1:03:15.536
I'm not standing on the edge.
I am already falling down!

1:03:15.539 --> 1:03:18.379
What are you, like, 23, 24?

1:03:18.377 --> 1:03:21.437
Young, fit as a fiddle,
immortal?

1:03:21.446 --> 1:03:23.606
All your death nonsense
is exactly that.

1:03:23.615 --> 1:03:26.675
A load of fucking nonsense!

1:03:26.685 --> 1:03:30.315
Step into the light more,
enjoy nice things.

1:03:30.321 --> 1:03:32.521
Stop skulking around
big holes in the ground

1:03:32.524 --> 1:03:35.234
and wasting your life
in all-night cafes.

1:03:35.227 --> 1:03:38.927
Enough with the facade,
this idle fucking fantasy!

1:03:38.930 --> 1:03:41.560
Go on, Bill. Go on, rage.

1:03:41.566 --> 1:03:44.466
Rage against the dying
of the fucking light!

1:03:44.468 --> 1:03:46.968
Did all this death stuff
start when mommy died?

1:03:48.372 --> 1:03:49.572
Ah, yeah.

1:03:49.573 --> 1:03:52.313
What was it,
an absent father?

1:03:52.310 --> 1:03:53.980
A concerned priest, perhaps?

1:03:53.979 --> 1:03:56.109
Did you find it was easier
to get attention

1:03:56.113 --> 1:03:58.113
if you were the freak,
the weirdo,

1:03:58.115 --> 1:04:02.145
the angel-faced kid
with a heart of darkness?

1:04:02.153 --> 1:04:05.123
I bet you were a cutter,
weren't you?

1:04:05.122 --> 1:04:07.192
I bet you loved
a good razor blade.

1:04:07.191 --> 1:04:10.191
Somewhere obvious where
everyone could see the scars.

1:04:10.194 --> 1:04:12.434
Did you have a little friend,
a little accomplice?

1:04:12.430 --> 1:04:14.700
Somebody you could go off
behind the bike shed with

1:04:14.700 --> 1:04:17.070
and burn each other
with cigarettes?

1:04:17.068 --> 1:04:19.468
Another little orphan helper
built in your own image,

1:04:19.470 --> 1:04:21.370
the two of you
egging each other on?

1:04:21.372 --> 1:04:24.042
Fuck! It's textbook, Annie!

1:04:24.042 --> 1:04:25.512
Textbook!

1:04:25.510 --> 1:04:27.980
You're two a penny!

1:04:27.979 --> 1:04:29.579
I have taught dozens of you
over the years.

1:04:29.580 --> 1:04:34.180
I have known silly little girls
like you all my life!

1:04:34.185 --> 1:04:39.515
Naughty, naughty little girls
just like you!

1:04:43.095 --> 1:04:44.255
Naughty.

1:04:48.232 --> 1:04:50.702
I just enjoy watching
you fidget when I say...

1:04:50.702 --> 1:04:52.442
Naughty.

1:04:54.339 --> 1:04:55.269
Gotcha.

1:04:56.508 --> 1:04:57.638
Oh, God!

1:04:59.577 --> 1:05:01.607
Have we met before?

1:05:03.115 --> 1:05:05.075
You remember now.

1:05:05.082 --> 1:05:07.122
Don't you,
Mr. Braithwaite?

1:05:07.118 --> 1:05:09.748
I think I would definitely
remember you if we'd met before.

1:05:09.754 --> 1:05:12.624
You would thing so,
wouldn't you?

1:05:12.624 --> 1:05:15.664
You remember this
naughty little girl?

1:05:17.328 --> 1:05:20.258
You remember punishing me,
Mr. B?

1:05:20.265 --> 1:05:22.195
Silly, naughty little girls,
enough!

1:05:22.200 --> 1:05:25.570
Maybe it's divine retribution.
You know, my sins revisiting me.

1:05:25.569 --> 1:05:27.139
I'm sorry.

1:05:27.138 --> 1:05:31.108
After lights out,
our little secret.

1:05:31.109 --> 1:05:34.579
Did something happen to you
as a child?

1:05:36.714 --> 1:05:40.154
I've waited all night
for you to remember me.

1:05:41.352 --> 1:05:43.822
All fucking night,

1:05:43.821 --> 1:05:47.491
not two feet away,

1:05:47.492 --> 1:05:51.392
just waiting for you
to connect the dots.

1:05:51.396 --> 1:05:53.756
Do you wanna know why
you don't have the balls

1:05:53.765 --> 1:05:57.125
to kill yourself,
Mr. Braithwaite?

1:05:57.135 --> 1:06:01.595
Because you know exactly where
you're going when you die.

1:06:05.209 --> 1:06:08.609
Orphans always make the best
victims, don't they, William?

1:06:08.613 --> 1:06:10.313
But chalk-stained fingers
leave indelible marks

1:06:10.314 --> 1:06:12.154
on little girls' panties.

1:06:13.484 --> 1:06:16.094
Consider this
divine retribution.

1:06:24.729 --> 1:06:26.669
Burn in hell.

1:06:35.841 --> 1:06:39.641
Was that gun loaded,
the one you pointed at me?

1:06:39.644 --> 1:06:42.444
<i>Impossible to say
either way.</i>

1:06:45.617 --> 1:06:47.717
- What's that?
- It's the fucking phone.

1:06:47.718 --> 1:06:48.688
All right.

1:06:53.725 --> 1:06:55.285
Yes?

1:06:55.292 --> 1:06:57.362
Okay.

1:06:57.361 --> 1:06:58.331
Got it.

1:07:01.533 --> 1:07:03.673
That was Mr. fucking Franklin.
It's on.

1:07:11.810 --> 1:07:12.750
Yeah.

1:07:20.385 --> 1:07:21.745
Yes?

1:07:21.752 --> 1:07:24.262
<i>Is this phone in range?</i>

1:07:28.526 --> 1:07:30.286
Where's the fucking target?

1:07:30.294 --> 1:07:31.834
Why aren't you
taking a shot?

1:07:31.830 --> 1:07:33.560
There is no shot.

1:07:33.564 --> 1:07:35.304
Take the shot, Vince.
What's the problem?

1:07:35.300 --> 1:07:36.640
Shut up!

1:07:39.271 --> 1:07:40.771
Bottle blonde!

1:07:40.772 --> 1:07:42.812
Fuck hell's she doing here?

1:07:42.807 --> 1:07:45.177
<i>Gotcha.</i>

1:07:49.414 --> 1:07:51.754
Put the gun down, Boss.

1:07:59.624 --> 1:08:01.494
What the fucking hell's
going on?

1:08:01.493 --> 1:08:04.893
This is what we call
in the trade "a double-cross."

1:08:04.896 --> 1:08:07.226
<i>Now put the gun down.</i>

1:08:07.231 --> 1:08:10.501
<i>And now sit at the table,
hands where I can see them.</i>

1:08:15.307 --> 1:08:16.437
You all right, bottle blonde?

1:08:16.440 --> 1:08:18.340
<i>Took your time, sweetheart.</i>

1:08:18.342 --> 1:08:20.342
<i>Thought you actually were
gonna let him have a pop at me.</i>

1:08:20.345 --> 1:08:22.975
Oh, I think he's been trying
that quite enough recently.

1:08:22.980 --> 1:08:24.280
<i>Stop it, Alfred.</i>

1:08:24.281 --> 1:08:25.421
Don't be naughty.

1:08:25.417 --> 1:08:26.777
<i>Sorry, sugarplum.</i>

1:08:26.784 --> 1:08:28.754
Now get yourself over here.

1:08:28.753 --> 1:08:31.763
Come and savor
this moment with me.

1:08:35.293 --> 1:08:37.433
I see you finally lost
your virginity then.

1:08:37.428 --> 1:08:39.428
Congratulations.

1:08:46.503 --> 1:08:47.843
Hi, handsome.

1:08:51.976 --> 1:08:53.436
You smell different.

1:08:53.445 --> 1:08:54.835
My new perfume.

1:08:54.846 --> 1:08:56.406
It's intoxicating.

1:08:56.413 --> 1:08:58.413
Oh, Jesus Christ, kill me now.

1:08:58.415 --> 1:08:59.475
With pleasure.

1:08:59.484 --> 1:09:02.624
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

1:09:02.620 --> 1:09:04.690
Tell me something.

1:09:04.689 --> 1:09:06.529
What have I ever
done to you, eh?

1:09:08.693 --> 1:09:10.963
Vincent Escariot.

1:09:10.962 --> 1:09:12.892
Tut, tut, tut.

1:09:12.896 --> 1:09:14.626
You'd sell your own partner
down the river

1:09:14.632 --> 1:09:16.572
for 30 pieces of silver.

1:09:16.568 --> 1:09:18.998
I like loyalty I can buy.

1:09:19.003 --> 1:09:21.343
You traitor, you.

1:09:22.841 --> 1:09:25.471
What the fuck's it got
to do with you?

1:09:25.476 --> 1:09:29.006
Now, now, Vince,
don't be rude.

1:09:29.013 --> 1:09:31.013
I think you've been
quite rude enough

1:09:31.016 --> 1:09:32.976
to my other half recently.

1:09:32.984 --> 1:09:34.984
Your girlfriend's doing all
your thinking now, is she?

1:09:34.985 --> 1:09:37.485
Well, fuck you...

1:09:37.489 --> 1:09:39.859
and your fucking whore.

1:09:39.857 --> 1:09:43.057
Don't you misunderstand
the situation you're in

1:09:43.061 --> 1:09:45.301
for one second, Vincent.

1:09:45.297 --> 1:09:46.997
You'll keep a civil tongue
in your head,

1:09:46.998 --> 1:09:48.598
or it won't be quick and easy.

1:09:48.600 --> 1:09:50.500
It'll be slow and messy.

1:09:50.502 --> 1:09:53.372
You are a fucking
pain in my ass!

1:09:53.370 --> 1:09:54.640
As well as being
a double-crossing,

1:09:54.638 --> 1:09:58.338
backstabbing,
turncoat traitor.

1:09:58.342 --> 1:10:00.542
But guess what.

1:10:00.544 --> 1:10:02.814
I've got a new partner now,
Vincent.

1:10:02.814 --> 1:10:05.424
And unlike with you,

1:10:05.417 --> 1:10:08.947
I just love it
when she fucks me.

1:10:08.953 --> 1:10:11.593
This is your doing,
isn't it, bottle blonde?

1:10:11.588 --> 1:10:13.758
Oh, yes, Vincent.

1:10:13.757 --> 1:10:16.017
I'm the master villain.

1:10:16.026 --> 1:10:18.996
Fucking crazy.

1:10:18.997 --> 1:10:22.097
The pair of you,
you're both mad, delusional.

1:10:22.100 --> 1:10:25.400
Fuck you
and your fucking whore!

1:10:25.403 --> 1:10:28.313
You don't have to let him
talk to us like that, handsome.

1:10:31.042 --> 1:10:32.912
No.

1:10:38.550 --> 1:10:40.890
Your eyes. I saw them...

1:10:43.654 --> 1:10:46.024
Bye, Vince.

1:10:49.860 --> 1:10:52.060
- That was fun.
- It was brilliant.

1:10:54.598 --> 1:10:57.368
Right. I need a shower
and a change of clothes,

1:10:57.369 --> 1:10:59.429
and then I'm taking you
out to dinner.

1:10:59.436 --> 1:11:00.696
My treat.

1:11:00.704 --> 1:11:03.774
Our first proper date.

1:11:03.775 --> 1:11:05.875
Bye-bye, sugarplum.

1:11:11.449 --> 1:11:13.389
Bye, handsome.

1:11:41.079 --> 1:11:43.749
Ah! Cleaning service.

1:11:45.516 --> 1:11:47.776
I'll have the works,
please, mate.

1:11:47.785 --> 1:11:50.485
The full spit and polish.

1:11:53.792 --> 1:11:55.632
Here's a cherry on top.

1:11:56.694 --> 1:11:59.464
Call it an apologetic token

1:11:59.463 --> 1:12:02.473
for the little overreaction
the other night, eh?

1:12:05.869 --> 1:12:09.139
See you later, Supe.

1:12:17.515 --> 1:12:18.775
Ohh...

1:12:30.794 --> 1:12:32.504
Hi, handsome.

1:12:32.497 --> 1:12:34.097
Hello, sugarplum.

1:12:39.904 --> 1:12:41.974
Did you get
your homework done?

1:12:41.972 --> 1:12:44.742
- Top of the class.
- Smart girl!

1:12:44.742 --> 1:12:47.642
I've got a little
surprise for you.

1:12:47.645 --> 1:12:50.075
Are you wearing that stripper
getup under that red coat?

1:12:50.080 --> 1:12:51.520
Stockings, suspenders?

1:12:54.785 --> 1:12:58.485
You know, you really do
have such a lovely jaw.

1:13:01.758 --> 1:13:04.588
Wait right here.

1:13:04.596 --> 1:13:06.456
Yeah.

1:13:33.223 --> 1:13:34.193
Hello?

1:13:43.066 --> 1:13:44.166
Sugarplum.

1:13:47.105 --> 1:13:48.105
Sugarplum.

1:13:51.275 --> 1:13:54.105
I really hate that nickname.

1:13:54.111 --> 1:13:57.711
Drop the gun,
hands up where I can see them.

1:13:57.714 --> 1:13:59.554
One wrong move, handsome,

1:13:59.551 --> 1:14:01.221
you'll have that gaping
exit wound in your face

1:14:01.218 --> 1:14:03.218
we talked about.

1:14:03.221 --> 1:14:04.761
Drop it.

1:14:06.925 --> 1:14:08.525
Kick it away.

1:14:10.861 --> 1:14:12.201
Good boy.

1:14:13.664 --> 1:14:15.064
I thought we were partners.

1:14:15.065 --> 1:14:16.765
I've already got a partner.

1:14:18.302 --> 1:14:21.272
Cripple?

1:14:21.271 --> 1:14:23.071
So all of this was, what?

1:14:23.074 --> 1:14:26.184
An overelaborate scheme
perpetrated mercilessly upon you

1:14:26.177 --> 1:14:29.137
by highly motivated, highly
intelligent individuals...

1:14:29.146 --> 1:14:31.676
With a penchant
for amateur dramatics.

1:14:31.682 --> 1:14:32.722
It's pronounced <i>penchant.</i>

1:14:34.151 --> 1:14:36.721
You are correct, Alfred.

1:14:36.721 --> 1:14:39.621
Two weeks you had me
in that fucking apartment,

1:14:39.623 --> 1:14:42.863
waiting to kill someone
who was waiting to kill me.

1:14:42.860 --> 1:14:44.960
- Why?
- Because we like to have

1:14:44.962 --> 1:14:46.902
all our dollies
lined up on the shelf.

1:14:46.897 --> 1:14:48.197
Shit!

1:14:48.199 --> 1:14:50.769
Our starving rats
locked in a cage,

1:14:50.767 --> 1:14:53.237
tearing each other apart
just for our pleasure.

1:14:54.771 --> 1:14:58.641
And... you never
really liked me?

1:14:58.642 --> 1:15:00.852
Me? No.

1:15:02.279 --> 1:15:04.779
Has anyone ever told you

1:15:04.781 --> 1:15:07.221
that you are a two-faced,

1:15:07.217 --> 1:15:09.887
treacherous, manipulative,

1:15:09.887 --> 1:15:12.787
callous little bitch?

1:15:12.789 --> 1:15:15.729
Oh, you have no idea.

1:15:19.364 --> 1:15:23.004
Annie, darling, I don't
suppose you'd consider...

1:15:26.837 --> 1:15:27.967
No.

1:15:36.748 --> 1:15:39.648
Look, I know
you wanted to keep him,

1:15:39.650 --> 1:15:42.420
but we got bigger
fish to fry, okay?

1:15:42.419 --> 1:15:45.619
I've got the ID papers.
Give me his gun.

1:15:48.426 --> 1:15:51.086
Stand and deliver!

1:15:51.095 --> 1:15:52.995
Oh, Christ!

1:15:52.997 --> 1:15:55.197
You nearly gave me
a heart attack.

1:15:57.935 --> 1:16:00.395
You're early.

1:16:00.404 --> 1:16:02.204
Give me that gun.

1:16:02.205 --> 1:16:04.305
Where'd you put Vincent?

1:16:07.145 --> 1:16:08.805
What you gonna do
with them both?

1:16:11.048 --> 1:16:14.048
Can we chuck them
in the river?

1:16:14.052 --> 1:16:15.292
No.

1:16:17.187 --> 1:16:19.757
I've got a better idea.
Give me a hand.

1:16:38.943 --> 1:16:41.443
Ah, for a fool such as this.

1:16:41.445 --> 1:16:45.205
I shall think nothing
of tumbling downstairs.

1:16:45.216 --> 1:16:47.946
Curiouser and curiouser.

1:16:51.855 --> 1:16:53.385
See you around, Supe.

1:16:53.391 --> 1:16:54.561
Oh, good day.

1:19:42.493 --> 1:19:43.903
Yes?

1:19:45.162 --> 1:19:48.062
<i>It's done, Mr. Franklin.</i>

1:19:48.065 --> 1:19:50.125
- <i>Yes?</i>
- Both of them.

1:19:50.133 --> 1:19:51.373
<i>Good.</i>

1:19:51.369 --> 1:19:55.269
And the little favor,
the teacher?

1:19:55.272 --> 1:19:57.312
I'm forever in your debt.

1:19:57.307 --> 1:19:59.467
Did you have fun, sweetie?

1:19:59.476 --> 1:20:01.136
It was like jelly and ice cream.

1:20:01.145 --> 1:20:02.605
<i>The cripple was very useful.</i>

1:20:02.613 --> 1:20:04.983
End of the Line cafe.

1:20:04.981 --> 1:20:06.651
- He's just the messenger.
- Mum's the word.

1:20:06.650 --> 1:20:08.480
- All right, son?
- Cleaning service.

1:20:08.485 --> 1:20:10.285
He has his uses.

1:20:10.288 --> 1:20:12.988
Are you suitably impressed,
Mr. Franklin?

1:20:14.557 --> 1:20:16.017
Most definitely.

1:20:16.026 --> 1:20:17.286
<i>Good.</i>

1:20:17.294 --> 1:20:19.364
So I can rely
on your business then?

1:20:19.363 --> 1:20:22.703
I have a limited
range of choice.

1:20:22.699 --> 1:20:26.239
You've suppressed
the competition admirably.

1:20:28.239 --> 1:20:31.339
How do I know you're not
going to double-cross me?

1:20:31.342 --> 1:20:33.142
<i>You seem very adept at it.</i>

1:20:33.144 --> 1:20:35.544
<i>How, indeed. But remember,</i>

1:20:35.546 --> 1:20:37.646
<i>I like loyalty I can buy,</i>

1:20:37.647 --> 1:20:40.477
<i>and you are unique.</i>

1:20:40.484 --> 1:20:43.394
<i>You're one of a kind.</i>

1:20:43.387 --> 1:20:45.887
You have proved
your value to me.

1:20:47.658 --> 1:20:52.588
So is this the start of
a beautiful relationship then?

1:20:52.596 --> 1:20:55.126
Most definitely.

1:20:56.700 --> 1:20:58.640
- Good night.
- <i>Good night.</i>

1:21:17.154 --> 1:21:18.994
404.

1:21:18.989 --> 1:21:20.319
Excellent.

1:21:39.709 --> 1:21:41.439
What do you want?

1:21:41.445 --> 1:21:43.075
There are two things in life

1:21:43.079 --> 1:21:45.419
for which we are never
truly prepared.

1:21:48.552 --> 1:21:49.492
Twins.

1:21:58.262 --> 1:22:01.602
Well, well, well, he lives.

1:22:03.667 --> 1:22:07.337
I'm sorry, Mr. Franklin,
is the light bothering you?

1:22:12.342 --> 1:22:13.742
Where am I?

1:22:13.744 --> 1:22:16.184
You like what we've
done with the place?

1:22:26.589 --> 1:22:29.389
A woman's touch
is what was needed.

1:22:29.392 --> 1:22:32.162
How... How the fuck did you...

1:22:32.163 --> 1:22:35.103
Look through the looking glass,
Mr. Franklin.

1:22:35.098 --> 1:22:37.728
Or shall we call you...

1:22:37.735 --> 1:22:39.425
Clinton?

1:22:39.436 --> 1:22:41.496
A rose by any other name.

1:22:41.504 --> 1:22:43.774
You've tumbled down
the rabbit hole

1:22:43.774 --> 1:22:46.544
far beyond hope
or rhyme or reason,

1:22:46.543 --> 1:22:48.613
flushed away
in a river of tears.

1:22:48.611 --> 1:22:51.551
You're mad!
Stark raving mad!

1:22:51.548 --> 1:22:53.278
Oh, we can't help that,
said the cat.

1:22:53.284 --> 1:22:54.584
We're all mad here.

1:22:54.584 --> 1:22:56.194
I'm mad. You're mad.

1:22:57.320 --> 1:22:58.850
Have you ever read it?

1:22:58.855 --> 1:23:00.085
It's our favorite book.

1:23:01.425 --> 1:23:04.225
Tweedledum and Tweedledee.

1:23:04.227 --> 1:23:06.387
Mommy used to read it to us
every night.

1:23:06.396 --> 1:23:08.096
We know it front to back,
cover to cover.

1:23:08.098 --> 1:23:09.558
Inside and out.

1:23:09.566 --> 1:23:11.526
If you gave us
a page and a line,

1:23:11.534 --> 1:23:14.104
we could give you the words,
verbatim.

1:23:14.105 --> 1:23:15.465
We hear tell it's hereditary.

1:23:15.472 --> 1:23:16.672
Like eye color.

1:23:16.673 --> 1:23:18.473
Or homicidal impulse.

1:23:18.476 --> 1:23:20.406
Blood will out.

1:23:20.410 --> 1:23:23.780
May we tell you a story,
Mr. Franklin?

1:23:23.780 --> 1:23:27.380
Are you sitting comfortably?

1:23:27.383 --> 1:23:29.693
- Then let us begin.
- Then let us begin.

1:23:31.387 --> 1:23:35.587
A long time ago in a place
not dissimilar to this,

1:23:35.592 --> 1:23:39.462
as a point of fact,
identical to this,

1:23:39.462 --> 1:23:45.132
there lived a young woman
called Chloe Merriweather.

1:23:45.136 --> 1:23:48.636
Now, Chloe Merriweather
had a gleam in her eye.

1:23:48.638 --> 1:23:52.138
She wanted adventure.

1:23:52.142 --> 1:23:55.612
One night in the aptly named
Anything Goes,

1:23:55.613 --> 1:23:58.153
Chloe Merriweather
succumbed to the wiles

1:23:58.149 --> 1:24:01.179
of one Clinton Sharp,
a low-level criminal

1:24:01.185 --> 1:24:03.645
with aspirations of grandeur,

1:24:03.654 --> 1:24:06.694
who whispered sweet nothings
in her ear

1:24:06.690 --> 1:24:10.760
and kept her drink topped up
and his powder dry.

1:24:10.761 --> 1:24:14.801
Theirs was a knee-trembling
relationship.

1:24:14.797 --> 1:24:18.327
Then for a time, very little
was heard of Chloe Merriweather

1:24:18.334 --> 1:24:21.344
until a year or so later
she reappeared.

1:24:21.337 --> 1:24:24.867
She'd grown up,
like all little girls do.

1:24:24.874 --> 1:24:28.314
She waited tables by day,

1:24:28.311 --> 1:24:30.581
and she danced on them
by night.

1:24:30.580 --> 1:24:34.680
For Chloe had a secret
that nobody knew

1:24:34.685 --> 1:24:37.585
buried deep within
her heart of hearts.

1:24:37.587 --> 1:24:41.317
She had two little girls
at home.

1:24:41.324 --> 1:24:42.894
Twins.

1:24:42.892 --> 1:24:46.232
The result of her passionate
tryst with Mr. Sharp.

1:24:48.766 --> 1:24:50.466
- Daddy.
- Daddy.

1:24:53.803 --> 1:24:56.873
But Chloe Merriweather knew
better than to involve Clinton

1:24:56.873 --> 1:24:58.913
in her daughters' lives,

1:24:58.909 --> 1:25:02.539
for she had seen
the shadow in his soul,

1:25:02.546 --> 1:25:04.406
the murder in his eyes.

1:25:07.717 --> 1:25:09.977
She kept them hidden
from the world

1:25:09.986 --> 1:25:12.486
and from Clinton Sharp.

1:25:12.489 --> 1:25:15.619
Deliciously sweet
were those times.

1:25:15.626 --> 1:25:18.726
But life is cruel,
and the world is small,

1:25:18.729 --> 1:25:21.629
and fate laughs mercilessly
at us all.

1:25:21.632 --> 1:25:25.772
One deep, dark night,

1:25:25.769 --> 1:25:30.539
Chloe Merriweather saw something
she ought not to have seen.

1:25:33.409 --> 1:25:35.779
Clinton Sharp working.

1:25:43.520 --> 1:25:46.850
Chloe Merriweather
ran for her life

1:25:46.856 --> 1:25:49.856
through that deep, dark night.

1:25:51.494 --> 1:25:54.664
But it wasn't long
before Clinton Sharp

1:25:54.664 --> 1:25:57.374
came calling for Chloe

1:25:57.368 --> 1:25:59.668
with a canister of petrol

1:25:59.669 --> 1:26:01.709
and his cigarette lighter.

1:26:06.877 --> 1:26:10.577
Rumor has it
he whistled while he worked.

1:26:15.686 --> 1:26:18.546
But Chloe Merriweather
was a fighter,

1:26:18.555 --> 1:26:20.815
a wildcat with fierce tears,

1:26:20.824 --> 1:26:23.594
unwilling to go gently
into that good night.

1:26:23.593 --> 1:26:25.893
Chloe saved her little girls,

1:26:25.895 --> 1:26:29.355
but the wildcat could not
get herself to safety.

1:26:39.043 --> 1:26:43.413
And so it was we found ourselves
wards of the precinct,

1:26:43.413 --> 1:26:45.653
taken into the mercy
and kindness

1:26:45.649 --> 1:26:48.479
of St. Catherine's Orphanage.

1:26:48.485 --> 1:26:51.885
To the welcoming arms of
the priests and the teachers

1:26:51.888 --> 1:26:54.858
with their wandering hands
and their sticky fingers.

1:26:54.857 --> 1:26:58.787
Here we learned how to close
our eyes and bite our lips.

1:26:58.796 --> 1:27:01.456
We learned how to go elsewhere
in our hearts and our heads

1:27:01.464 --> 1:27:03.564
when the lights went out.

1:27:03.566 --> 1:27:05.566
As soon as our legs
would carry us,

1:27:05.569 --> 1:27:07.899
we ran far, far away.

1:27:07.904 --> 1:27:10.544
Survival was
all we hoped for.

1:27:10.540 --> 1:27:12.470
A feral existence.

1:27:12.476 --> 1:27:15.506
Until one day,
who should we see

1:27:15.512 --> 1:27:19.012
shuffling by with his cart
and his broom and his limp,

1:27:19.016 --> 1:27:20.546
but Clinton Sharp.

1:27:24.387 --> 1:27:27.817
In all his crippled glory.

1:27:27.824 --> 1:27:30.134
That selfsame whistle

1:27:30.127 --> 1:27:33.397
that had haunted
our nightmares for so long.

1:27:37.767 --> 1:27:40.067
So we hunted you, Daddy,

1:27:40.070 --> 1:27:44.040
and before long, we discovered
your clever little secret.

1:27:44.040 --> 1:27:49.380
Mr. Franklin,
a master villain marionette.

1:27:49.379 --> 1:27:52.609
The legendary black briefcases,
the infamous voice messages,

1:27:52.615 --> 1:27:55.145
the lost art of mystery.

1:27:55.151 --> 1:27:57.051
What's in it?

1:27:57.053 --> 1:27:59.023
Another fucking
locker number.

1:27:59.021 --> 1:28:02.761
Oh, you gotta love
Mr. Franklin, don't you?

1:28:02.760 --> 1:28:05.060
Who says mystery's a lost art?

1:28:05.061 --> 1:28:07.131
Who says
mystery's a lost art?

1:28:07.131 --> 1:28:10.731
And we let you track us, Daddy,
as we tracked you.

1:28:10.734 --> 1:28:13.774
Inch by inch,
we laid our plans against you.

1:28:13.770 --> 1:28:16.770
We baited our traps
and cast our lures.

1:28:19.109 --> 1:28:22.579
We pulled the strings
that made you dance.

1:28:22.579 --> 1:28:25.579
We knew exactly
what would get your attention

1:28:25.582 --> 1:28:31.192
and that you couldn't resist
hearing our confession.

1:28:31.187 --> 1:28:36.087
I need a teeny, weeny donation,
Mr. Nigel Illing.

1:28:36.092 --> 1:28:40.132
<i>Mr. Franklin, I must confess,
I've been a naughty girl.</i>

1:28:40.129 --> 1:28:42.429
<i>Meet me at
St. Catherine's Church.</i>

1:28:42.432 --> 1:28:45.032
This is
a well-conceived venue.

1:28:45.034 --> 1:28:48.474
I want your work,
your contracts, all of it.

1:28:48.471 --> 1:28:50.101
I'm afraid you're out of luck.

1:28:50.106 --> 1:28:53.806
I've been recommended
another interested party

1:28:53.811 --> 1:28:55.141
to take care of my problems.

1:28:55.145 --> 1:28:57.805
I'm better.

1:28:57.815 --> 1:28:59.805
I highly doubt it.

1:28:59.816 --> 1:29:04.846
You men, with your bad suits
and your pumiced hair,

1:29:04.855 --> 1:29:07.855
you're utterly predictable.

1:29:07.857 --> 1:29:10.127
I reckon to the point
of carelessness.

1:29:10.127 --> 1:29:11.527
Yes.

1:29:11.528 --> 1:29:12.888
Me?

1:29:12.895 --> 1:29:15.825
I'm the switchblade
in the garters,

1:29:15.833 --> 1:29:18.833
the stiletto in the stilettos.

1:29:18.836 --> 1:29:22.596
I'm the surprise
they never see coming.

1:29:22.605 --> 1:29:25.605
Who says mystery's a lost art?

1:29:25.609 --> 1:29:27.509
Who'd have thought?

1:29:27.511 --> 1:29:29.451
We're Daddy's little girls,
after all.

1:29:35.052 --> 1:29:37.522
And now we stand on
the brink of our vengeance,

1:29:37.520 --> 1:29:40.560
on the cusp
of the wildest of justice.

1:29:41.691 --> 1:29:44.961
You are my daughters, yeah?

1:29:44.962 --> 1:29:47.602
In blood only, Daddy.

1:29:47.597 --> 1:29:49.197
Don't get too attached.

1:29:49.199 --> 1:29:51.669
Mommy has to be avenged.

1:29:51.668 --> 1:29:54.698
Tell us, Daddy, are you familiar
with the science of lobotomy?

1:29:54.704 --> 1:29:56.714
Much maligned
in this day and age,

1:29:56.707 --> 1:29:59.567
but somehow rather
fitting in this scenario,

1:29:59.575 --> 1:30:00.575
don't you think?

1:30:00.577 --> 1:30:02.507
Please, girls.

1:30:02.512 --> 1:30:04.712
Anything.
I'll do anything.

1:30:04.714 --> 1:30:07.224
But not this, please!
Not this.

1:30:07.217 --> 1:30:10.587
I beseech you
in your mother's name!

1:30:10.587 --> 1:30:12.017
I am your father!

1:30:12.021 --> 1:30:15.291
No, no, no.
Far too little, far too late.

1:30:15.292 --> 1:30:17.632
Shh, Daddy, easy.

1:30:17.628 --> 1:30:20.128
I've got you.
Try not to fight.

1:30:20.129 --> 1:30:22.129
The time has come,
the walrus said,

1:30:22.132 --> 1:30:24.062
to speak of many things,

1:30:24.066 --> 1:30:27.766
like shoes and ships
and sealing wax,

1:30:27.770 --> 1:30:30.170
cabbages and kings.

1:30:37.146 --> 1:30:39.776
An eye for an eye, Daddy.

1:30:47.324 --> 1:30:49.764
The coup de grâce
is yours, dear sister.

1:30:49.760 --> 1:30:51.560
The nail in the coffin.

1:30:55.565 --> 1:30:57.925
Send Mr. Franklin
to Wonderland.

1:31:06.743 --> 1:31:08.043
Night-night, Daddy.

1:31:18.922 --> 1:31:20.892
- Perfect.
- Perfect.

1:32:29.675 --> 1:32:33.825
Subtitles by explosiveskull
